r/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Applies Travis’s 2026-11-16 choices for D635, D636, D638, D648 and D651 to the sync branch. Tracks #2312, #2277 and #1532.\n\n- D635: move all six model-discovery cases below TOML validation and construct the provider directly. Keep user/app precedence, replacement-manager behavior, bundled/remote catalog assertions and no-fetch checks. Custom providers still cannot use the reserved OpenAI name.\n- D636: current-settings resume sends the current provider; update the resume expectations and ensure the retry fixture allows disk provider changes instead of pinning its server to a test default.\n- D638: hide Vertex/Bedrock Runtime onboarding entries when their flags are off; cover all four flag combinations and keep the wizard navigation checks. Port the held-Enter row to the shared provider flow and apply its activation guard to provider API-key rows.\n- D648: every V2 thread receives manager tools regardless of catalog metadata; the native-tools off switch still wins.\n- D651: detached children remain denied, with a message telling the user to open the parent and reopen the child. The lifecycle fixture opens the parent first; a separate test verifies refusal and no model request.\n\nCore hunks are limited to `tools/spec_plan.rs`, `client.rs` and `security/effective_policy.rs`, coordinated on #1532 before editing. D621 #2390 and permission persistence #2387 are included in the base merge. D642/D643 and D644/D647 are untouched. This is an S4 compile/runtime fix under `docs/management/upstreamSyncPlan.md`, not SG2 qualification. It follows `docs/corbanu-product-spec.md`, Product definition: retain upstream capabilities while preserving Corbanu provider and security behavior.\n\nValidation on Rust 1.99.1:\n- Local focused tests: **103 TUI + 6 app-server passed**, no failures or ignored tests.\n- `just fix -p codex-app-server -p codex-tui -j8 --no-deps` passed; owned Rust files formatted; release-note check/preview passed (108 fragments).\n- `just fmt` is blocked by existing sync CLI conflict markers. The same blocker remains outside this PR.\n- First glitch build reproduced the assigned baseline failures. The second/final glitch build passed **103 TUI + 6 app-server** tests with `-j10` in the same source/target pair. Both builds are used; no third build will run. The subsequent review correction changes only two test files; production code is unchanged from the Linux-tested head.\n- Fail-before evidence also includes the new detached-child message assertion without the fix, and the provider-key held-Enter test before adding its guard.\n\nOpus round 1 requested an update to the existing core D648 matrix and restoration of OpenAI-menu held-Enter coverage. The test-only correction passed locally (core matrix 1 test / 4 cases, activation 2 tests). **Opus round 2 APPROVE** on exact head `d006b4dc9decd4ae6b613fdb12cf8ad5fec8cf1f`; [corbanu-security approval](https://github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/pull/2393#pullrequestreview-5916951731) records that same SHA in both commit and body. Review budget 2/2 used. All CI checks must complete and sync-base reds be documented before merge.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-16T08:00:38Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T09:21:20Z","closed_at":"2026-11-16T09:21:20Z","merged_at":"2026-11-16T09:21:20Z","merge_commit_sha":"0e962a492222f907c3317659166a057e5892ff97","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"CorbanuCore:astra-syncdec1","ref":"astra-syncdec1","repo":{"id":1283517261,"node_id":"R_kgDOTIDrTQ","name":"CorbanuTerminal","full_name":"CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal","owner":{"login":"CorbanuCore","id":315989408,"node_id":"O_kgDOEtWdoA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/315989408?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CorbanuCore","html_url":"https://github.com/CorbanuCore","followe